  "subject": {
    "id": "derivation-rule-reach-digest-modality-and-locality",
    "type": "DOCUMENT"
  },
  "summary": "Check what a derivation points at: recompute the statement digest, require an evaluating assertion for an evaluative slot, and report derivation locality and fan-out.",
  "why": "handover/2026-09-05-run-04-review-rca.md. The derivation rule binds every value to an assertion; the adapter enforced the binding's existence, never its content. All 104 of run-04's located claims carried a correct statement_sha256 and nothing recomputed one; rel:069 carried 36 targets for twelve relations whose endpoints it names none of, and the largest hubs formalize 47 and 23 records from single sentences; all five dispositions derive from the HYPOTHESISED sentence that raises the hypothesis, never the one that disposes of it. DIGEST_MISMATCH and UNKNOWN_ASSERTION_LOCATOR recompute the digest from the located assertion's statement bytes, in one aggregated refusal. research 0.4.0 adds enum HypothesisDisposition, slot hypothesis_disposition and the mixin Evaluative worn by Claim, whose slot list declares which slots are evaluative; the adapter takes the compiled contract as an eighth argument and refuses EVALUATIVE_SLOT_NOT_EVALUATED when only HYPOTHESISED assertions formalize one. No modality was added. The census gains a closed derivation block: fan-out, relation locality, the distribution, the top hubs and the non-local count, reported and never refused."
}
